In classic mode, PARAM(), QUERY(), HEADER() and BODY() read the current
request (Requirement 7.3). Header names are lowercase, as in req.headers
(Requirement 7.2), and BODY() is {} when there is no body, as req.body is.

### all four helpers
POST /graves/13?sort=oldest
X-Token: boo

{"name": "Vlad"}
=> 200

{"id": "13", "sort": "oldest", "token": "boo", "name": "Vlad"}

### each request sees its own values
POST /graves/7?sort=newest
X-Token: eek

{"name": "Casper"}
=> 200

{"id": "7", "sort": "newest", "token": "eek", "name": "Casper"}

### BODY() with no body
GET /graves/1
=> 200

{"id": "1", "body": {}}
